    "notes": "Q849241/way251331418 identifies the exact temple. Twenty-two PMTiles building components retain their original vertices: main outline, U-shaped cella wall, podium, eleven stair parts, column bases, all18 shafts and roof/entablature bands. The mapped stair projection and ordinary front picture fix the north-northwest front; the rear photograph confirms four engaged rear columns. Geometry retains raw east/south coordinates at heading0, with an internal162.695-degree architectural rotation so local+Z faces north-northwest. Reviewed approximate full-site fit on the unchanged161-square/6m standard DEM. Twenty-two mapped temple components retain241 original control vertices, including18 shaft positions, cella wall, podium, eleven stair parts and roof/entablature bands. The mapped stair projection and two ordinary photographs establish the north-northwest front; geometry retains raw east/south coordinates at heading0, with a162.695-degree internal architectural rotation. Six columns are free-standing and twelve engaged. The lower datum is the least offset that keeps every mapped stair above its original terrain by0.2m; this lowers the initial conservative draft by about0.546m. For all12 occupied floors,76 intersecting original terrain triangles were clipped to the floor footprints and290 resulting corners evaluated; minimum clearance is0.200000017m. Retaining sides extend below coarse grade. Tiny upper-floor clipping scraps under0.1m² were removed to eliminate false stair-side spikes; all original controls remain unchanged. No ground/water cutout. Full loading replaces22 authored records and preserves1356 independent tile buildings exactly; all2491 independent buildings in the retained extract stay outside the replacement envelope. Source retains63 nearby records, including the22 controls. Twelve native water records retain203489.55596715916 square metres. Failed loads preserve all1378 native tile buildings; eviction frees all model geometry. Synthetic10m residency clips the portico/stairs, rear cella and pediments, exposing floor/roof edges while keeping original ground under and around the partial architecture. Full completeness requires surrounding tiles; exposed partial floors are not approved as a complete temple. Independent neighboring monuments retain native procedural shells in this single-landmark fixture; their historical appearance is not approved. Ionic carving, fluting, door, exact stucco loss, roof pitch and thresholds remain medium-fi estimates.",
    "groundContactBasis": "Reviewed approximate full-site fit on the unchanged161-square/6m standard DEM. Twenty-two mapped temple components retain241 original control vertices, including18 shaft positions, cella wall, podium, eleven stair parts and roof/entablature bands. The mapped stair projection and two ordinary photographs establish the north-northwest front; geometry retains raw east/south coordinates at heading0, with a162.695-degree internal architectural rotation. Six columns are free-standing and twelve engaged. The lower datum is the least offset that keeps every mapped stair above its original terrain by0.2m; this lowers the initial conservative draft by about0.546m. For all12 occupied floors,76 intersecting original terrain triangles were clipped to the floor footprints and290 resulting corners evaluated; minimum clearance is0.200000017m. Retaining sides extend below coarse grade. Tiny upper-floor clipping scraps under0.1m² were removed to eliminate false stair-side spikes; all original controls remain unchanged. No ground/water cutout. Full loading replaces22 authored records and preserves1356 independent tile buildings exactly; all2491 independent buildings in the retained extract stay outside the replacement envelope. Source retains63 nearby records, including the22 controls. Twelve native water records retain203489.55596715916 square metres. Failed loads preserve all1378 native tile buildings; eviction frees all model geometry. Synthetic10m residency clips the portico/stairs, rear cella and pediments, exposing floor/roof edges while keeping original ground under and around the partial architecture. Full completeness requires surrounding tiles; exposed partial floors are not approved as a complete temple. Independent neighboring monuments retain native procedural shells in this single-landmark fixture; their historical appearance is not approved. Ionic carving, fluting, door, exact stucco loss, roof pitch and thresholds remain medium-fi estimates."
